# 🚨 CRITICAL: Fix Occupant Load Calculation System

## Executive Summary

**SEVERITY**: **CRITICAL** - Life Safety Compliance Issue
**STATUS**: Non-compliant with CAS2 Section 1.4.2
**IMPACT**: All CA/WB/WS/VP firecells have incorrect occupant loads, resulting in potentially incorrect fire safety system requirements

### The Problem

The current system asks users to **manually enter** occupant loads for ALL risk groups. This is **fundamentally incorrect** for CA/WB/WS/VP risk groups per CAS2 Section 1.4.2, which mandates:

> "**Occupant loads shall be calculated from the occupant densities given in Table 1.2 based on the floor area** of the part of the building housing the activity."

**Only SM and SI** use bed spaces (manual entry). **All other risk groups MUST calculate** occupant load from floor area and activity density.

### Current vs. Correct Behavior

| Risk Group | Current (WRONG ❌) | Correct (CAS2 ✅) |
|------------|-------------------|-------------------|
| **SM/SI** | Manual entry (correct for bed spaces) | ✅ Manual entry - Bed spaces |
| **CA/WB/WS/VP** | Manual entry ❌ | ✅ **CALCULATE**: floor area ÷ density |

