## 📖 Regulatory Requirements Analysis

### CAS2 Section 1.4 - Calculating Occupant Loads (Pages 37-39)

#### Section 1.4.2 (Page 37):
> "**Occupant loads shall be calculated from the occupant densities given in Table 1.2 based on the floor area** of the part of the building housing the activity."

**Interpretation**: This is **mandatory** ("shall"), not optional. Calculation required for all activities with numeric densities.

#### Table 1.2 - Occupant Densities (Pages 38-39):

| Activity | Density | Calculation Required? |
|----------|---------|----------------------|
| **Sleeping non institutional** | **Bed spaces** | ❌ NO - Direct count |
| **Care and detention** | **Bed spaces, see Para 1.4.6** | ❌ NO - Direct count |
| Office spaces | 10 m²/person | ✅ **YES** - floor area ÷ 10 |
| Classrooms | 2 m²/person | ✅ **YES** - floor area ÷ 2 |
| Retail spaces | 3.5 m²/person | ✅ **YES** - floor area ÷ 3.5 |
| Parking buildings, garages | 50 m²/person | ✅ **YES** - floor area ÷ 50 |
| Bulk storage | 100 m²/person | ✅ **YES** - floor area ÷ 100 |
| *(All other activities)* | *(Numeric densities)* | ✅ **YES** - Calculate |

#### Section 1.4.5 (Page 37):
> "The requirements of this Acceptable Solution account for the fact that other people may be present in the building or firecell and **additional calculations are not required when an occupant load is derived by bed spaces** (i.e. for **risk groups SM and SI**)."

**Key Points**:
- SM/SI are **explicitly exempt** from calculation
- Bed spaces already account for staff, visitors, etc.
- **Implication**: All OTHER risk groups MUST calculate

#### Section 1.4.6 (Page 37):
For SI (care/detention), "bed" includes beds, chairs, treatment tables, etc. where people are under care or detention.

